---

<CaseStudy
  title="R50"
  subtitle="A small building with a very sociable edge."
  heroPlaceholder="R50 hero — wraparound balcony facade (photo needed)"
  facts={facts}
  gallery={gallery}
  prev={{ href: '/spreefeld/', label: 'Spreefeld, Berlin' }}
  next={{ href: '/sargfabrik/', label: 'Sargfabrik' }}
>
  <section class="case-reading mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-6 pt-12 sm:px-12">
    <p>R50 is a 19-home collective housing project in Berlin-Kreuzberg, completed in 2013 by ifau, Jesko Fezer, and Heide & von Beckerath. Its shared rooms and continuous exterior balconies make a compact building an interesting cousin of the courtyard block, even though it is not a full perimeter court. <a class="source-link" href="https://www.ifau.berlin/projects/r50">[Project source]</a></p>
    <p>A Baugruppe is a group that commissions a building together. It describes a development process, not automatically a limited-equity cooperative or a promise of permanent affordability. R50 is useful here because it asks what residents can decide together at a relatively small scale.</p>
    <h2>Hello from the balcony. Or just a wave.</h2>
    <p>An exterior edge can support informal contact without requiring everyone to attend dinner. The design question is how to pair that contact with privacy: windows, passing neighbors, sound, plants and places to sit. A continuous balcony should not be confused with the building’s legally approved escape route.</p>
    <p>For another city, put an accessible apartment plan and a fire strategy beside the attractive balcony sketch. Then ask residents which shared spaces they actually want to pay for. There is no universal ideal number of homes or neighbors.</p>
    <aside class="research-note mt-8">Reading lens: project publications document the place and its intended design. They are not independent evaluations of affordability, energy performance or how every resident experiences life there. The questions here are our interpretation.</aside>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="lessons">
<li>Make residents a real design client, with decision support and time for disagreement.</li>
<li>Distinguish balconies, access galleries and required exits; each has different duties.</li>
<li>Check entry costs and resale rules separately from resident involvement. A group-built home can still be expensive.</li>
</Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sources"><a href="https://www.ifau.berlin/projects/r50">ifau · R50 project record</a>. Reviewed October 2026. Approximate counts are identified; population changes over time.</Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
